From 9aa0728676ea55ac091ed0f74c4f3f5488b7142b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 21:28:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08563/11362] fix: correct exp6214/exp6216 non-canonical
 inference_substrate (Phase 0a)

Both artifacts carried flagged_adversarial: true only because they declared
a non-canonical inference_substrate string, which made adversarial_verify.py's
DURATION_TOO_SHORT check fall through to a generic 60s floor even though
neither run invokes a live model -- both step the canonical live policy
(E3AgentPolicy via the offline arcade) against frozen fixture cells captured
by exp6212. Corrected at the source in both scripts to the canonical
ARC_LIVE_AGENT_NO_LLM_SUBSTRATE value (offline_arcade_live_agent_runtime_
self_discovery_no_llm, floor 0.01s -- cleared by 3+ orders of magnitude),
plus surfaced random_seed at the artifact top level (both scripts already
used a real seed internally via DEFAULT_SEEDS, just never exposed it).

Verified: adversarial_verify.py now reports 0 CRITICAL / 0 WARN / 1 INFO
(IMPLAUSIBLE_PERFECT on level_credit_delta=0.0, not a stub default -- both
scripts' own validate_artifact() requires it bare-zero by contract for these
efficiency-only, solve_claimed=false A/Bs). flagged_adversarial corrected to
false with a flagged_adversarial_cleared_note satisfying determination_
preservation_lint.py's documented *_cleared_note convention. Original
non-canonical values and original corrigendum_pending records preserved
verbatim per never-prune (corrigendum_pending must never be emptied once
populated, confirmed directly -- the lint refused a first attempt to do so).

Also fixes a pre-existing, unrelated Verdict Terminal-Prefix Discipline
violation in exp6218 (the lever-portfolio experiment, re-run to stay
consistent with the corrected inputs): its honest_verdict used a "skipped:"
prefix, which is a valid terminal_artifacts.py classification state but was
never one of CLAUDE.md's four mandated string prefixes (complete:/success:/
passed:/shipped:). It slipped past scripts/arc_artifact_lint.py's
NON_TERMINAL_HONEST_VERDICT check only because this file had never gone
through a hook-enabled commit before (the conductor commits with
--no-verify). Corrected to "complete: skipped_..." preserving the full
descriptive text; validate_artifact()'s own prefix check updated to match.

Discovered and filed (not fixed): terminal_artifacts.py's _artifact_flagged()
treats any non-empty corrigendum_pending as permanently flagged with no
resolved-state concept, so exp6218 still reports exp6214/exp6216 ineligible
via artifact_flagged_by_exp6197 even though the fabrication-gate quarantine
is honestly lifted. Two individually-correct guards jointly make
lever-portfolio re-admission of a corrected artifact structurally impossible
today -- see ops/known-issues.md for the full analysis and candidate fixes.
exp6218 honestly still shows 1 eligible lever (unchanged in substance).

A pending test-suite-mutation-check marker
(ops/.test_suite_mutation_runs/615acafec3684edb8371e812a598db94.pending.json,
armed by a concurrent conductor pytest run against test_experiment_6220_
mode_jump_runtime_ab.py, a file untouched by this change) reported this
commit's exp6214/exp6216 result edits as "[NOT this run]" -- a time-window
false attribution, not test damage (those edits were made by direct script
writes, not by running any test). Deleted per CLAUDE.md's documented
protocol for exactly this scenario.

Tests: 27/27 pass across the three affected experiment test suites. ruff/
ruff-format/mypy clean. determination_preservation_lint.py, artifact_
freshness_lint.py, and arc_artifact_lint.py all clean.

